# MasjidConnect Display App — Project Overview

## What This Application Is

A **digital signage application** for mosques. Screens display:

- Prayer times (Adhan and Jamaat) with countdown to next prayer
- Announcements and events
- Emergency alerts (full-screen overlay)
- Islamic content (Hadith, Quranic verses)

## Critical Design Constraints

| Constraint | Detail |
|---|---|
| **No user input** | End users never interact with the display (except initial QR-code pairing) |
| **Offline-first** | Must work reliably without internet — cached data is always available |
| **Always-on** | Runs 24/7 on Raspberry Pi; must self-heal from errors without manual intervention |
| **Low-powered hardware** | Primary target is Raspberry Pi 4 — every render and allocation matters |
| **Display-only** | Global `cursor: none`, no scrollbars, no text selection, kiosk mode |

## Current Tech Stack

| Layer | Technology |
|---|---|
| Framework | React 18 + TypeScript 5 |
| Build tool | Vite 7 (`@vitejs/plugin-react`) |
| Styling | Tailwind CSS v4 (`@tailwindcss/vite`) — CSS-based config, NO `tailwind.config.js` |
| State | Redux Toolkit + Redux Persist (localStorage) |
| Real-time | Socket.io-client + custom `realtimeService` |
| HTTP | Axios with retry + offline fallback |
| Storage | LocalForage (IndexedDB) → localStorage fallback |
| PWA | `vite-plugin-pwa` with Workbox service worker |
| Icons | `lucide-react` |
| Date/time | `date-fns` + `dayjs` |
| Runtime | **Chromium kiosk mode** on Raspberry Pi — NOT Electron |

> **Electron has been removed.** The app is a standard Vite SPA served by a lightweight
> Node.js static server (`deploy/server.mjs`) and displayed in Chromium kiosk mode.
> Do NOT add Electron dependencies or reference Electron APIs.

## Data Flow

```
API (portal.masjidconnect.co.uk)
  ↓
API Client (src/api/masjidDisplayClient.ts | apiClient.ts)
  ↓
Redux Async Thunks (contentSlice, authSlice)
  ↓
Redux Store (src/store/index.ts)
  ↓ ←→ Middleware (realtimeMiddleware, emergencyMiddleware)
  ↓
Redux Persist → localStorage
  ↓
React Components ← Custom Hooks + Selectors
```

## Storage Hierarchy

1. **LocalForage** (IndexedDB via `storageService`) — primary for large/cached data
2. **localStorage** (via Redux Persist) — persisted Redux state
3. **In-memory cache** (Map inside API clients) — request deduplication, short TTL

## Directory Structure

```
src/
├── api/                 # API clients, models, endpoints
├── assets/              # Logos, fonts, SVG patterns
├── components/
│   ├── screens/         # Top-level phase screens (Loading, Pairing, Display)
│   ├── layout/          # Orientation wrappers (Landscape, Portrait, OrientationWrapper)
│   └── display/         # Reusable display pieces (Header, Footer, PrayerTimesPanel, etc.)
├── config/              # Environment configuration (wraps import.meta.env)
├── hooks/               # Custom React hooks
├── services/            # Singleton service layer
├── store/
│   ├── slices/          # Redux slices (auth, content, ui, emergency)
│   ├── middleware/       # Custom middleware (realtime, emergency)
│   ├── hooks.ts         # Typed useAppDispatch / useAppSelector
│   └── index.ts         # Store configuration + persist setup
├── types/               # Global type declarations
├── utils/               # Logger, date utils, admin URL utils
├── App.tsx              # Root component — routing, error boundary, emergency overlay
├── main.tsx             # Entry point — Provider, PersistGate
└── index.css            # Tailwind import + @theme design tokens + global styles
deploy/
├── server.mjs           # Node.js static file server (port 3001)
├── kiosk.sh             # Chromium kiosk launcher
├── install.sh           # Raspberry Pi installation script
└── *.service            # systemd unit files
scripts/                 # Build, optimisation, and validation scripts
.github/workflows/       # CI/CD — build for ARM, create .deb, publish GitHub Release
```

## Custom Hooks (use these — do NOT reimplement)

| Hook | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `useAppLoader` | App lifecycle phases: `startup` → `pairing` → `loading` → `ready` |
| `usePrayerTimes` | Prayer time calculations, current/next prayer, Hijri date |
| `useCurrentTime` | Reactive current time (updates every second) |
| `useConnectionStatus` | Network and WebSocket connection state |
| `useRotationHandling` | Physical vs desired orientation, CSS rotation logic |
| `useDevKeyboard` | Development-only keyboard shortcuts (Alt+1–7 for alerts, Escape to clear) |

## Services (all singletons — import the default export)

| Service | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `storageService` | Persistent storage via LocalForage with localStorage fallback |
| `syncService` | Periodic data sync with backend, debounced polling |
| `credentialService` | Screen pairing credentials — normalises multiple storage formats |
| `realtimeService` | WebSocket/SSE connection management |
| `emergencyAlertService` | Emergency alert handling and expiry tracking |
| `networkStatusService` | Online/offline detection with event emitter |
| `remoteControlService` | Remote command handling from admin portal |

## Path Alias

`@/` maps to `src/` (configured in `vite.config.ts` and `tsconfig.json`).

```typescript
import logger from '@/utils/logger';
import usePrayerTimes from '@/hooks/usePrayerTimes';
```
